# task_diagnostics/ is a nested checkout of the PRIVATE rc-eval repo, tracked there, not here.
# Keep the whole directory out: without this git adds it as a gitlink, which publishes the
# private repo's URL and commit id on a public remote. A negation cannot re-include anything
# under it either -- files inside an excluded directory are never reachable.
task_diagnostics/

# Internal-only: infra paths + unpublished analysis. Public repo -- keep out of git.
docs/GRID5000.md
reasoning_core/task_search/README.providers.private.md
# reports/: internal. The tooling names infra paths, hosts and unpublished measurements, and
# build/ holds result snapshots and queue telemetry. Keep the whole directory off the public remote.
reasoning_core/reports/
# ...and the test that imports it.
tests/test_difficulty_tune.py
